4682.9s 249 The paper used its own data; our numbers are on the 498R All-in-One test split (different data),
4682.9s 250 so the comparison shows the direction and size of the gap, not a head-to-head result.
4682.9s 251 
4682.9s 252 Different labels: the paper's are human legibility judgements on Brazilian traffic-radar plates; ours are OCR-difficulty labels from two cross-fitted readers on Bangla plates, so the F1 rows show the direction only. The useful number for us is the gate: plate exact of the plates we accept vs the OCR's own confidence.
